**The last step requires you to do it manually** (it needs your Packagist login):

### Register on Packagist

1. Go to **https://packagist.org/**
2. Sign in with your GitHub account
3. Click **"Submit"** (top right)
4. Paste your repo URL: `https://github.com/ApiratN/boost`
5. Click **"Check"** → then **"Submit"**

Packagist will index it automatically, and within a minute this will work:

```bash
composer require apiratn/boost
```

### Alternative: if you don't want to use Packagist

In any project that needs this package, add this to `composer.json`:

```json
"repositories": [
    {
        "type": "vcs",
        "url": "https://github.com/ApiratN/boost"
    }
]
```

Then run:
```bash
composer require apiratn/boost:^2.0
```

This works **immediately** without Packagist registration.[0m
